issues.fix_hint:
Replace handleDrop's body with a single synchronous call:

  void readDroppedFiles(e.dataTransfer, { accept: WEB_RDF_ACCEPT, readFile: decompressReader }).then(onIngest);

(readDroppedFiles already extracts the File objects before its first await, so the synchronous-extraction requirement is met.) Then export a small `readFiles(files, opts)` from file-ingest.ts — it is already the shared helper, just module-private — and call it from handleInputChange with the same options object, deleting readFilesWithDecompress entirely. That removes ~35 lines and both duplicated literals, and makes the drop path covered by the new tests instead of merely resembling them. If you keep the local copies, at minimum export and call rejectedReasonUnsupported so the message has one definition.

Special-case HDT before the generic accept check in readFilesWithDecompress:

  if (isHdt(file.name)) { rejected.push({ name: file.name, reason: "HDT archives are native-only — open this file in the desktop app" }); continue; }

isHdt is already exported from rdf-format.ts and correctly handles .hdt.gz, so this also fixes the .hdt.gz slip-through. Separately, decide deliberately about the tightening: either widen WEB_RDF_ACCEPT with the other extensions the engine parses as turtle (.n3, .rdf, .owl), or note the intentional narrowing in gui/README.md so the behaviour change is recorded rather than incidental.
